{"doc_id":"DDC-076","file":"LINKS_DDC-076.tsv","header":["src_doc","src_page","text","n","kind","target_doc","target_page","target_page_end","target_pin","target_quote","status","by","note"],"rows":[{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"1","text":"Local Civil Rule 7","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Local Rules AUG_2025","target_page":"29","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"LCvR 7","status":"verified","target_quote":"Each motion shall include or be accompanied by a statement of the specific points of law and authority that support the motion, including where appropriate a concise statement of facts. If a table of cases is provided, counsel shall place asterisks in the margin to the left of those cases or authorities on which counsel chiefly relies.","line":2,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-1-1-1-d0d103b8","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":29,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"1","text":"paragraph 7.c of the Court's Civil Standing Order (Mar. 4, 2026)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"2026.03.04 FINAL CIVIL STANDING ORDER (ACR)","target_page":"4","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 7.c","status":"verified","target_quote":"Sur-Replies. A party may not file a sur-reply without first obtaining leave of the Court","line":3,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-1-1-1-6df189c2","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"1","text":"paragraph 7.c","n":"2","kind":"rule","target_doc":"2026.03.04 FINAL CIVIL STANDING ORDER (ACR)","target_page":"4","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 7.c","status":"verified","target_quote":"A party may not file a sur-reply without first obtaining leave of the Court and may do so only upon a specific showing of good cause. Any motion for leave to file a sur-reply shall not be accompanied by a copy of the sur-reply that the party wishes to file.","line":4,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-1-2-1-2278f136","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"1","text":"ECF No. 75","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-075","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 75","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":5,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-1-1-1-d9c583b7","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"1","text":"ECF No. 74","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-074","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 74","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":6,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-1-1-1-a6e6ba82","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"1","text":"ECF 74 at 15 ¶ 16","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-074","target_page":"15","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 15 ¶ 16","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":7,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-1-1-1-5d69d242","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":15,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"1","text":"Lewis v. Rumsfeld, 154 F. Supp. 2d 56, 61 (D.D.C. 2001)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"","target_page":"","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"154 F. Supp. 2d at 61","status":"unresolved","target_quote":"","line":8,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-1-1-1-be3823bb","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":null,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":false,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"1","text":"Ben-Kotel v. Howard Univ., 319 F.3d 532, 536 (D.C. Cir. 2003)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"2003 - Ben-Kotel v. Howard University, 319 F.3d 532 (D.C. Cir. slip, No. 01-7155)","target_page":"7","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"319 F.3d at 536 (slip 7)","status":"verified","target_quote":"As the University points out, Ben-Kotel could have apprised the district court of his evidence of Ms. Thiere's possible re-employment by moving for leave to file a sur-reply. The district court routinely grants such motions when a party is ''unable to contest matters presented to the court for the first time'' in the last scheduled pleading. Lewis v. Rumsfeld, 154 F. Supp. 2d 56, 61 (D.D.C. 2001)","line":9,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-1-1-1-56addaf6","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"2","text":"Herbert v. Nat'l Acad. of Scis., 974 F.2d 192, 196 (D.C. Cir. 1992)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"1992 - Herbert v. National Academy of Sciences, 974 F.2d 192","target_page":"196","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 196","status":"verified","target_quote":"This Court, of course, generally refuses … to entertain arguments raised for the first … time in an appellant's reply brief. See, e.g., … United States v. Caicedo-Llanos, 960 F.2d … 158, 164 (D.C.Cir.1992); Golden Pacific … Bancorp v. Clarke, 837 F.2d 509, 513 … (D.C.Cir.1988); McBride v. Merrell Dow … and Pharmaceuticals, Inc., 800 F.2d 1208, … 1211 (D.C.Cir.1986); Environmental … Fund, Inc. v. Costle, 657 F.2d 275, … 284 n. 32 (D.C.Cir.1981); United States v … Haldeman, 559 F.2d 31, 78 n. 113 … (en banc) (per curiam), cert. denied, … 431 U.S. 933, 97 S.Ct. 2641, 53 L.Ed.2d 250 … (1977); see also Fed.R.App.P. 28(a)(4). The … reasons for our rule on this score are … and plain. To consider an argument … discussed for the first time in reply would … written response. Moreover, it would risk … the possibility \"of an improvident or … opinion,\" given our dependence as … an Article III court on the adversarial … process for sharpening the issues for … McBride, 800 F.2d at 1211","line":10,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-2-1-1-80909645","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"2","text":"McBride v. Merrell Dow & Pharms., Inc., 800 F.2d 1208, 1211 (D.C. Cir. 1986)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"","target_page":"","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"800 F.2d at 1211","status":"unresolved","target_quote":"","line":11,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-2-1-1-91b89410","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":null,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":false,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"2","text":"Standing Order ¶ 7.c","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"2026.03.04 FINAL CIVIL STANDING ORDER (ACR)","target_page":"4","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 7.c","status":"verified","target_quote":"upon a specific showing of good cause","line":12,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-2-1-1-70cf0e91","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"2","text":"ECF No. 70-1","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-070-01","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 70-1","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":13,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-2-1-1-e165e333","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":"2","text":"MTD 54-56","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-070-01","target_page":"54","target_page_end":"56","target_pin":"at 54-56","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":14,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-076-2-1-1-64498831","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":54,"target_pdf_page_end":56,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-076","src_page":